# Workflow

Before marking a task complete:

1. `docker compose build` from repo root — **this is the only automated test run** we use to verify the tree (frontend `tsc` + Vite, backend image).
2. `npm run check:lines` — fix or split any production file over the **200**-line cap.

Do **not** run `npm run check` / Vitest / pytest as part of routine agent finish unless the user explicitly asks. Still add or update unit tests in code when behavior changes (they are not run every turn).

If you changed Docker, nginx, or auth and the user wants a live check: `docker compose up --build -d` then `npm run test:smoke`.

When adding or changing behavior:

- Add or update tests in the same change when practical.
- After each feature slice, add at least one regression test if coverage is thin.
- When touching stable code without tests, add a minimal test before or as part of the change.

Keep production files **~120 lines**; never exceed **200** without splitting first.
